The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```dts
&gpio0 {
	ti,no-idle-on-init;
	ti,no-reset-on-init;
```
Reason:
The flags `ti,no-idle-on-init` and `ti,no-reset-on-init` were incorrectly placed at the GPIO0 node level instead of the interconnect target module level. This misplacement caused warnings about the flags needing to be at the module level, which could lead to improper initialization behavior for the GPIO0 module.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```dts
&gpio0_target {
	ti,no-reset-on-init;
```
Reason:
By moving the `ti,no-reset-on-init` flag to the `&gpio0_target` node, the flags are now correctly defined at the interconnect target module level. This change resolves the warnings and ensures proper initialization behavior for the GPIO0 module.

